    },
    {
      "session_id": "fb5d6697-a064-46a5-9e62-b6711ca54870",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Paracetamol (Acetaminophen)**\n\n\u2022 Uses: Reduces fever, relieves mild to moderate pain (headache, toothache, muscle aches)\n\u2022 Dosage: Adults: 500-1000mg every 4-6 hours, max 4000mg/day. Children: 10-15mg/kg every 4-6 hours\n\u2022 Side effects: Nausea, rash, liver damage (with overdose), allergic reactions\n\u2022 Interactions: Warfarin (increased bleeding risk), Alcohol (increased liver toxicity), Carbamazepine\n\u2022 Storage: Store below 25\u00b0C, protect from light\n\nAlways follow your doctor or pharmacist's instructions and the label. This is educational information, not medical advice.",
      "created_at": "2026-08-09T14:42:50.391453+00:00"
    },
